From f3f42b2ddc6d7a18cc3cf28a6d9e506186221338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nuthasith G <nuthasith.g@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:58:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Make quad-fisheye cross-camera tracking work on the CPU
 build

- opticalflowTrackPyr (CPU) ignored the shifted start points; pass OPTFLOW_USE_INITIAL_FLOW
  as the GPU path already does, so cross-camera LK finds matches at all
- TrackReport::compose now sums stereo_point_num
- cross_cam_min_disparity: drop cross-camera matches too close to the far-point prediction,
  whose depth over a short baseline is noise and biased short
- cross_cam_guess_distance: optional depth-aware start point for cross-camera LK
- log the number of landmarks shared by neighbouring cameras once a second

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../include/d2frontend/d2featuretracker.h     |  6 ++-
 .../include/d2frontend/opticaltrack_utils.h   |  4 +-
 d2frontend/src/d2featuretracker.cpp           | 51 ++++++++++++++++---
 d2frontend/src/d2frontend_params.cpp          |  6 +++
 d2frontend/src/opticaltrack_utils.cpp         | 31 ++++++++---
 5 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

